# HTMX & Jinja2 Patterns

## HTMX Core Rules
- Use `hx-get` for data fetching from FastAPI endpoints
- Use `hx-target` to specify exactly where fragments land in the DOM
- Use `hx-trigger="load"` for initial data loads on page sections
- Never return full HTML pages from HTMX endpoints — fragments only
- Fragments live in `frontend/templates/partials/`

## Template Structure
- Every template must extend `base.html` using `{% extends "base.html" %}`
- `base.html` loads Tailwind (CDN) and HTMX (CDN)
- Section containers declare their `hx-get` target on page load

## Example section pattern
```html
<!-- In index.html -->
<section
  hx-get="/section/overview"
  hx-trigger="load"
  hx-target="#overview-content">
  <div id="overview-content">
    <!-- Fragment loads here -->
  </div>
</section>

<!-- In templates/partials/overview.html -->
<div>
  <!-- Content renders here -->
</div>
```

## Tailwind
- Utility classes only — no custom CSS unless absolutely necessary
- Use Tailwind's prose classes for narrative text sections

## ECharts (only if this project uses charts)
If the project includes data visualisation, load ECharts v5 in `base.html`:
```html
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/echarts/5.4.3/echarts.min.js"></script>
```

- Always use ECharts **v5** syntax
- Initialise charts with `echarts.init(el)` inside the partial's `<script>` block
- Always call `chart.resize()` on `window resize` to keep charts responsive
- Pass data from Jinja2 context using `{{ data | tojson }}`
- Use `echarts.graphic.LinearGradient` for area fills
- Use `markPoint` for annotating significant data points (min, max, key events)

```html
<!-- Example chart partial -->
<div id="overviewChart" style="width:100%;height:350px;"></div>
<script>
  const chart = echarts.init(document.getElementById('overviewChart'));
  chart.setOption({ /* ECharts v5 option object goes here */ });
  window.addEventListener('resize', () => chart.resize());
</script>
```
